## Universal Constitutional Audit Set

Every phase should use the same core audit vocabulary, regardless of domain:

| Audit                 | Purpose                                                 |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Ownership Audit       | Single constitutional owner per entity                  |
| Replay Audit          | Deterministic reconstruction from immutable artifacts   |
| Archaeology Audit     | Complete lineage and explainability                     |
| Determinism Audit     | Stable outputs, ordering, hashing, and serialization    |
| Dependency Audit      | Explicit dependency graph with no hidden cycles         |
| Boundary Audit        | No leakage into future phases or unrelated domains      |
| Evidence Flow Audit   | Immutable evidence pipeline with no bypasses            |
| Graph Integrity Audit | Structural correctness of graphs and relationships      |
| Serialization Audit   | Canonical encoding and hash stability                   |
| Validation Audit      | Campaign completeness and threshold checks              |
| Independent Audit     | Reproduction from evidence without runtime imports      |
| Long-Horizon Audit    | Stability and evolution over extended time horizons     |
| Readiness Audit       | Constitutional maturity for the next phase              |
| Certification Audit   | Final proof that all required gates have been satisfied |

This gives every future phase—from Mathematics (16.X) through World Modeling, Engineering Intelligence, and Civilizational Intelligence—the same constitutional lifecycle, making the entire Tiannara architecture consistent, predictable, and easier to audit and evolve.
